**Time/Space:** feed O(F + 10 log F) / O(users + tweets)

**Pitfall:** Self-follow/unfollow edge cases: a user must always see their own tweets.

**Pattern:** Two heaps

**Key insight:** A max-heap holds the smaller half and a min-heap the larger half; keep sizes within one so the median sits at the tops.

**Java**

```java
class MedianFinder {
    private final PriorityQueue<Integer> low = new PriorityQueue<>(Collections.reverseOrder());
    private final PriorityQueue<Integer> high = new PriorityQueue<>();
    public void addNum(int num) {
        low.offer(num);
        high.offer(low.poll());
        if (high.size() > low.size()) low.offer(high.poll());
    }
    public double findMedian() {
        if (low.size() > high.size()) return low.peek();
        return (low.peek() + (long) high.peek()) / 2.0;
    }
}
```

**Python**

```python
import heapq

class MedianFinder:
    def __init__(self):
        self.low = []   # max-heap (negated)
        self.high = []  # min-heap

    def addNum(self, num: int) -> None:
        heapq.heappush(self.low, -num)
        heapq.heappush(self.high, -heapq.heappop(self.low))
        if len(self.high) > len(self.low):
            heapq.heappush(self.low, -heapq.heappop(self.high))

    def findMedian(self) -> float:
        if len(self.low) > len(self.high):
            return -self.low[0]
        return (-self.low[0] + self.high[0]) / 2
```

**Time/Space:** add O(log n), median O(1) / O(n)

**Pitfall:** Pushing straight into one heap without routing through the other breaks the "low ≤ high" invariant.

**Pattern:** Backtracking (include / skip)

**Key insight:** At each index branch on taking or not taking the element; record the path at every node.

**Java**

```java
class Solution {
    public List<List<Integer>> subsets(int[] nums) {
        List<List<Integer>> res = new ArrayList<>();
        go(nums, 0, new ArrayList<>(), res);
        return res;
    }
    private void go(int[] nums, int start, List<Integer> path, List<List<Integer>> res) {
        res.add(new ArrayList<>(path));
        for (int i = start; i < nums.length; i++) {
            path.add(nums[i]);
            go(nums, i + 1, path, res);
            path.remove(path.size() - 1);
        }
    }
}
```

