**Pattern:** Backtracking with duplicate skipping

**Key insight:** Sort, move to i+1 after picking, and skip equal values at the same depth (`i > start && c[i] == c[i-1]`).

**Java**

```java
class Solution {
    public List<List<Integer>> combinationSum2(int[] candidates, int target) {
        Arrays.sort(candidates);
        List<List<Integer>> res = new ArrayList<>();
        go(candidates, 0, target, new ArrayList<>(), res);
        return res;
    }
    private void go(int[] c, int start, int left, List<Integer> path, List<List<Integer>> res) {
        if (left == 0) { res.add(new ArrayList<>(path)); return; }
        for (int i = start; i < c.length && c[i] <= left; i++) {
            if (i > start && c[i] == c[i - 1]) continue;
            path.add(c[i]);
            go(c, i + 1, left - c[i], path, res);
            path.remove(path.size() - 1);
        }
    }
}
```

